       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for inpatient use is 3,200 mg/day, so this is twice the limit. It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing, such as in rheumatologic conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours.** This is the usual dose for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
